Enable GSSAPI/Kerberos support in libcurl for the rsu build.

The OpenWrt curl package does not expose a kconfig switch for GSSAPI and
defaults to the autoconf `--without-gssapi`. The Negotiate proxy-auth code
path added in azure-c-shared-utility patch 0031 requires libcurl to be
built with GSSAPI; without it `CURLAUTH_NEGOTIATE` silently falls back to
Basic.

Add an unconditional `--with-gssapi="$(STAGING_DIR)/usr"` and pull
`krb5-libs` into libcurl's DEPENDS so the staging dir always has the
required headers/libs when libcurl builds.

This patch is applied from `feeds/packages/` (suffix `.patch-packages`).

--- a/net/curl/Makefile
+++ b/net/curl/Makefile
@@ -94,6 +94,7 @@ define Package/libcurl
   DEPENDS:= +LIBCURL_WOLFSSL:libwolfssl +LIBCURL_OPENSSL:libopenssl +LIBCURL_GNUTLS:libgnutls +LIBCURL_MBEDTLS:libmbedtls
   DEPENDS += +LIBCURL_ZLIB:zlib +LIBCURL_ZSTD:libzstd +LIBCURL_THREADED_RESOLVER:libpthread +LIBCURL_LDAP:libopenldap
   DEPENDS += +LIBCURL_LIBIDN2:libidn2 +LIBCURL_SSH2:libssh2 +LIBCURL_NGHTTP2:libnghttp2 +ca-bundle
+  DEPENDS += +krb5-libs
   TITLE:=A client-side URL transfer library
   MENU:=1
   ABI_VERSION:=4
@@ -120,6 +121,7 @@ CONFIGURE_ARGS += \
 	--without-libpsl \
 	--without-zstd \
 	--with-ca-bundle=/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt \
+	--with-gssapi="$(STAGING_DIR)/usr" \
 	\
 	$(call autoconf_bool,CONFIG_IPV6,ipv6) \
 	\
